# Line endings, so a clone on any OS gets a clean checkout and the first person
# to commit does not produce a whitespace-only diff across half the repo.
#
# The tree is mixed today (28 generated .json are CRLF, most sources are LF)
# because the generators run on Windows and git was never told what to do about
# it. `text=auto` normalises to LF in the repository and checks out whatever the
# platform wants, so this settles it once.
* text=auto

# PowerShell is happiest with CRLF on Windows, and these scripts are Windows-only
# by nature: they drive WolvenKit and the game install.
*.ps1 text eol=crlf

# Binary. Never normalise these, and never try to diff them as text.
*.wem   binary
*.archive binary
*.anims binary
*.ent   binary
*.png   binary
*.pdf   binary

# Generated resources. They are committed on purpose, so a clone can build
# without running anything, but a diff of a 12,588-line quest graph helps nobody.
# Marking them linguist-generated keeps them out of GitHub's language stats and
# collapses them in pull requests.
mods/*/source/wkit/raw/** linguist-generated=true
